VRANGE* MIN_ABS / MAX_ABS broke equal-magnitude ties by position instead of by sign

SDM (VRANGEPD/PS/SD/SS) Tables 5-24 and 5-25: when |src1| = |src2| and the
signs differ (including +0 / -0), MIN_ABS returns the negative operand and
MAX_ABS the positive one, whichever position it is in. f{16,32,64}_range
cleared signA for the absolute compare, so on a tie `tmp_a < tmp_b` was
false and MIN_ABS always returned src2, MAX_ABS always src1 — wrong whenever
src1 is the negative one, e.g. vrangeps imm8=06h on (-2, +2) gave +2.
Only visible with imm8[3:2] = 01 (sign of the compare result); the other
sign controls rewrite the sign bit, and on a tie that is all that differs.

signA now stays set on a tie, so the existing select picks by sign.

Backport of upstream commit 04b100ae1f ("fix VRANGE* output when both
arguments are different sign same magnitude ad ABS_MIN and ABS_MAX is
requsted", 2026-08-30), plus a comment. Upstream has it, so a re-vendor
at or past that commit should drop this patch.

diff --git a/cpu/softfloat3e/f16_range.cc b/cpu/softfloat3e/f16_range.cc
index 25bb1cc..6461c2f 100644
--- a/cpu/softfloat3e/f16_range.cc
+++ b/cpu/softfloat3e/f16_range.cc
@@ -107,7 +107,9 @@ float16 f16_range(float16 a, float16 b, bool is_max, bool is_abs, int sign_ctrl,
         if (is_abs) {
             tmp_a = tmp_a & ~0x8000; // clear the sign bit
             tmp_b = tmp_b & ~0x8000;
-            signA = 0;
+            // equal magnitudes: keeping signA makes MIN_ABS pick the negative one and MAX_ABS the positive one (SDM Table 5-25)
+            if (tmp_a != tmp_b)
+              signA = 0;
         }
 
         if (! is_max) {
